{
  "description": "Hand-written merge cases. scripts/vectors.mjs expands them into full rows and computes expected results with lib/merge-reference.mjs → merge.json (generated, never hand-edit). A side is `null` (row absent) or a patch on `base`: `set` columns, `stamp` groups with an HLC, `unstamp` groups (remove from field_hlc). Every group of `base` starts stamped with `base_hlc`. Frontiers default to the frontier of the side's own row (ADR 0017). More patch keys: `stamp_all` (stamp every group), `extra_stamp` (stamps for groups the spec does not know), `compacted` {hlc, deleted_at} (the tombstone compaction writes: contracts x-compact values, every group stamped with hlc), `raw` (override columns with invalid values), `omit` (drop columns). A case with `expect_error` must fail with that code.",
  "hlcs": {
